ory="XP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>ABEL EDWARD W. ET AL.: 'dynamic NMR studies of ring rotation in substituted ferrocenes and turhenocenes' J. ORGANOMET. CHEM., vol. 403, no. 1-2, 1991, pages 195 - 208, XP002929052</text><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>KAMIYAMA SHINICHI ET AL.: 'Synthesis of (3.3) (1,1')- and (5.5) (1,1')ruthenocenophanes and their ferrocenoruthenocenophane homologs' BULL. CHEM. SOC. JPN., vol. 54, no. 7, 1981, pages 2079 - 2082, XP002929053</text><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1083161A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA PRECIOUS METAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO, KOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA KIKINZOKU KOGYO K.K.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organoruthenium compound and an organoplatinum compound with each of which a thin film can be deposited at a constant rate and which have excellent thermal stability. The organoruthenium compound has a cyclopentadiene ring, which is a five-membered ring, having as at least one substituent an alkyl group selected among CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH2CH3, C(CH3)3, CH2(C6H5), COCH3, COOCH3, and CH2OCH3. The platinum compound has a cyclopentadiene ring, which is a five-membered ring, having as at least one substituent an alkyl group selected among CH3, CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH2CH3, C(CH3)3, and CH2(C6H5).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un composé organoruthénique et un composé organoplatinique se prêtant chacun au dépôt de film fin à débit constant, et présentant une excellente stabilité thermique. Le composé organoruthénique comporte un cyclopentadiène à cinq côtés, pour lequel l'un au moins des substituants est un groupe alkyle appartenant au groupe des CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH2CH3, C(CH3)3, CH2(C6H5), COCH3, COOCH3, et CH2OCH3. Le composé organoplatinique comporte un cyclopentadiène à cinq côtés, pour lequel l'un au moins des substituants est un groupe alkyle appartenant au groupe des CH3, CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH3, CH2CH2CH2CH3, C(CH3)3, et CH2(C6H5).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>